#### pub fn [title](#method.title)<T>(self, title: T) -> [Block](struct.Block.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Block")<'a>

where T: [Into](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")<[Line](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line")<'a>>,

Adds a title to the block using the default position.

The position of the title is determined by the `title_position` field of the block, which defaults to `Top`. This can be changed using the [`Block::title_position`](struct.Block.html#method.title_position "method ratatui::widgets::Block::title_position") method. For explicit positioning, use [`Block::title_top`](struct.Block.html#method.title_top "method ratatui::widgets::Block::title_top") or [`Block::title_bottom`](struct.Block.html#method.title_bottom "method ratatui::widgets::Block::title_bottom").

The `title` function allows you to add a title to the block. You can call this function multiple times to add multiple titles.

Each title will be rendered with a single space separating titles that are in the same position or alignment. When both centered and non-centered titles are rendered, the centered space is calculated based on the full width of the block, rather than the leftover width.

You can provide any type that can be converted into [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line") including: strings, string slices (`&str`), borrowed strings (`Cow<str>`), [spans](../prelude/struct.Span.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Span"), or vectors of [spans](../prelude/struct.Span.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Span") (`Vec<Span>`).

By default, the titles will avoid being rendered in the corners of the block but will align against the left or right edge of the block if there is no border on that edge. The following demonstrates this behavior, notice the second title is one character off to the left.

```
┌With at least a left border───

Without left border───
```

Note: If the block is too small and multiple titles overlap, the border might get cut off at a corner.

##### [§](#examples-1)Examples

See the [Block example](https://github.com/ratatui/ratatui/blob/main/examples/README.md#block) for a visual representation of how the various borders and styles look when rendered.

The following example demonstrates:

-   Default title alignment
-   Multiple titles (notice “Center” is centered according to the full with of the block, not the leftover space)
-   Two titles with the same alignment (notice the left titles are separated)

```
use ratatui::text::Line;
use ratatui::widgets::Block;

Block::bordered()
    .title("Title")
    .title(Line::from("Left").left_aligned())
    .title(Line::from("Right").right_aligned())
    .title(Line::from("Center").centered());
```

