#### pub fn [style](#method.style)<S>(self, style: S) -> [Block](struct.Block.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Block")<'a>

where S: [Into](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")<[Style](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style")\>,

Defines the style of the entire block.

This is the most generic [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") a block can receive, it will be merged with any other more specific styles. Elements can be styled further with [`Block::title_style`](struct.Block.html#method.title_style "method ratatui::widgets::Block::title_style") and [`Block::border_style`](struct.Block.html#method.border_style "method ratatui::widgets::Block::border_style"), which will be applied on top of this style. If the block is used as a container for another widget (e.g. a [`Paragraph`](struct.Paragraph.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Paragraph")), then the style of the widget is generally applied before this style.

See [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") for more information on how merging styles works.

`style` accepts any type that is convertible to [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") (e.g. [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style"), [`Color`](../prelude/enum.Color.html "enum ratatui::prelude::Color"), or your own type that implements [`Into<Style>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")).

##### [§](#example-5)Example

```
use ratatui::style::{Color, Style, Stylize};
use ratatui::widgets::{Block, Paragraph};

let block = Block::new().style(Style::new().red().on_black());

// For border and title you can additionally apply styles on top of the block level style.
let block = Block::new()
    .style(Style::new().red().bold().italic())
    .border_style(Style::new().not_italic()) // will be red and bold
    .title_style(Style::new().not_bold()) // will be red and italic
    .title("Title");

// To style the inner widget, you can style the widget itself.
let paragraph = Paragraph::new("Content")
    .block(block)
    .style(Style::new().white().not_bold()); // will be white, and italic
```

